'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... isp_dummy_flash.spin2
''   Purpose.... Flash image that announces a reboot from flash: not part of the HUB75 driver
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2022 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Mar 2022
''   Updated.... 02 Oct 2026
''
'' =================================================================================================
''
'' This program is flashed onto every P2 Edge board used for development. Demos and tests are
'' loaded into RAM and run from there; if a RAM-loaded run crashes and the board resets, it
'' boots from flash instead, and this program prints its greeting on the debug port. Seeing
'' "* Hi! from FLASH *" in a log therefore means the RAM-loaded program died and the board
'' rebooted. It is kept in this repository so it is compile-checked with everything else.
''

CON { timing }

  CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                        ' system freq as a constant
  _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ                                           ' set system clock

CON { fixed io pins }

  RX1      = 63  { I }                                          ' programming / debug
  TX1      = 62  { O }

  SF_CS    = 61  { O }                                          ' serial flash
  SF_SCK   = 60  { O }
  SF_SDO   = 59  { O }
  SF_SDI   = 58  { I }

PUB main()
'' Announce that the board has booted from flash, then hold.

    debug("* Hi! from FLASH *")

    repeat                                                      ' hold here; nothing else runs


